  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueManager
  PersonalityCompatibilityStregthList:
  - A: 0
    B: 1
    Strength: 8
  - A: 0
    B: 2
    Strength: 3
  - A: 0
    B: 3
    Strength: 4
  - A: 1
    B: 2
    Strength: 3
  - A: 1
    B: 3
    Strength: 6
  - A: 2
    B: 3
    Strength: 8
  OrderedEmojisCount: 48
  RandomCharSymbols: "?:-$%&@!+*=/#~^<>[]{}()|;,.`\"'\xBF\xA1\xA9\xAE\u2122\xA7\xB6\xB1\xD7\xF7\u221A\u221E\u2206\xB0\u203B#%&@!$^~+=-|<>[]{}"
  _tutorialLines:
  - This is the Tutorial, please press on the text to move on.
  - You're goal is to match robots together based on their connection.
  - You have to figure out how connected the robots are based on...
  - Their emoji based language, and their facial expressions.
  - If you feel that the vibes are good, press that Green Match button.
  - If not, press that Red Mutate button to randomize the robots' personalities and
    try again.
  - You have to be quick though, leave them talking too long and one of them might
    leave!
  - Your subconcious thoughts are also shown after you make decisions in the box
    above.
  - If you want to know how many more Attempts you have left, check the Green Battery.
  - If you want to know how many more good Matches you need to win, check the Red
    Battery..
  - That's all! Good luck and have fun!
  _storyLines:
  - You are a bad programmer who has found himself responsible for future of technology
    as we know it!
  - Through dumb luck you discovered that pairing two AI's together drastically increases
    performance.
  - However bad matches result in seriously dangerous power consumption!
  - And even worse the robots might decide to turn on us because of you.
  - 'Can you handle the challenge? Or will you doom us all with your horrible decisions... '
  _continueInput: {fileID: -2099379676528639254, guid: 2bcd2660ca9b64942af0de543d8d7100, type: 3}
